- op: create  # 9ed4
  at: '2026-08-04T23:41:41Z'  # 9ed4
  by: agent  # 9ed4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9ed4
  clock: 1  # 9ed4
  nonce: 9ed4  # 9ed4
  data:  # 9ed4
    kind: work_item  # 9ed4
    title: "External-symbol ids stamp the \"external\" sentinel instead of a module in 5 of 13 languages, capping dst_ref coverage at 60.4% and pinning the dst string parse permanently"  # 9ed4
    status: todo_hard  # 9ed4
    priority: 2  # 9ed4
    parent:  # 9ed4
    tags:  # 9ed4
    - adr_0037  # 9ed4
    - analysis_quality  # 9ed4
    - taint  # 9ed4
    isbefore: []  # 9ed4
    duplicate_of: []  # 9ed4
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 9ed4
    pr_ref:  # 9ed4
    description: "FOUND 2026-08-04 while re-scoping WI-lonad. Filed separately rather than folded\ninto it, because the fix belongs to the analyzers and WI-lonad's belongs to\ntaint -- folding would repeat the scope-axis error the re-scope exists to\ncorrect (L1).\n\nWHAT WAS MEASURED. 9-repo cohort (zoxide, express, SwiftyJSON, spring-petclinic,\napollo-server, caddy, pretix, alertmanager, kserve), full behavior maps, 13\nlanguages, population selected by production's own _is_taint_call_edge.\n\nOf 62,861 unresolved taint call edges, 24,889 (39.6%) carry dst_ref=None. ALL\n24,889 are explained by one mechanism: _derive_dst_ref_from_id\n(finalize.py:357-372) returns None when the dst id's path slot is the literal\n\"external\" sentinel, because WI-huzuv forbids promoting a sentinel to a\nfabricated module path. That refusal is CORRECT. The defect is upstream -- the\nproducers that stamp the sentinel in the first place.\n\ndst_ref coverage on the unresolved arm, by language:\n\n    typescript   96.9%        javascript   57.7%\n    bash        100.0%        python       50.7%\n    jsonnet     100.0%        rust         34.1%\n    go           72.6%        java         23.9%\n                              swift        16.2%\n                              fish          0.0%\n                              powershell    0.0%\n\nA ~6x spread on the SAME construct (a call to an external symbol) is the tell\nthat this is a per-analyzer emission convention, not a property of the\nlanguages. typescript, bash and jsonnet can name the external module; swift and\njava mostly cannot, and emit ids shaped\n\n    swift:external:0-0:<name>:external_symbol\n    java:external:0-0:<name>:external_symbol\n\nwhere a covered language emits\n\n    bash:mktemp:0-0:mktemp:external_symbol   -> ExternalRef(bash, mktemp, mktemp)\n\nWHY IT MATTERS BEYOND TIDINESS. Three consumers are capped by this, and none of\nthem can fix it locally:\n * WI-lonad's module re-key gains a typed module only where dst_ref exists, so\n   its reach is bounded by this table rather than by anything in taint.\n * ADR-0037's stated goal is that consumers stop parsing dst strings. With 39.6%\n   of the unresolved arm carrying no ref, the string parse cannot be retired --\n   it has to stay as a fallback indefinitely.\n * io_boundary module matching has the same dependency: an edge whose module is\n   the \"external\" sentinel carries no module evidence to match a catalog\n   primitive against, which is one reason bare-name collision guards\n   (ambiguous_names, WI-razol) are load-bearing at all.\n\nSCOPE, DELIBERATELY UNMEASURED HERE. Which analyzers CAN recover a module and\nare simply not doing it, versus which genuinely cannot (an unresolved bare call\non an untyped receiver may have no recoverable module at any cost). That\ndistinction decides whether this is a fixable emission gap or a disclosure, and\nit must be measured per analyzer BEFORE choosing a fix -- counting the sentinel\nrate is not the same as counting the recoverable subset, and reporting the\nformer as the latter is exactly the denominator error L60 warns about.\n\nDO NOT start by sweeping the analyzers. Establish first, on one language with a\nlow rate (swift at 16.2% or java at 23.9%), whether the module is present in the\nAST at the emission site. If it is not, this is a disclosure item, not a fix."  # 9ed4
    fields: {}  # 9ed4
- op: discuss  # 6d90
  at: '2026-08-05T00:59:56Z'  # 6d90
  by: agent  # 6d90
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6d90
  clock: 2  # 6d90
  nonce: 6d90  # 6d90
  message: "PREREQUISITE SHIPPED (PR #207, dev d1116cc1af). Raising external-id module coverage would, before that PR, have been actively harmful for Rust: taint truncated every colon-bearing module to its first component and _lookup_named_entry rejects on a mismatched module, so the 396 rust edges that currently arrive via the `external` sentinel (and therefore match) would have started carrying std::fs and been REFUSED - taking rust from 45 matched sinks to zero. The path slot now has one right-anchored parser, so that trap is closed and this item is safe to work. It is still the right item: 24,889 of 62,861 unresolved taint call edges carry no dst_ref, all of them explained by the sentinel, and the per-language spread (typescript 96.9 percent, swift 16.2 percent) is the evidence that this is an emission convention rather than a property of the languages."  # 6d90
