- op: discuss  # 468b
  at: '2026-09-06T15:45:17Z'  # 468b
  by: agent  # 468b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 468b
  clock: 6  # 468b
  nonce: 468b  # 468b
  message: "RE-MEASURED AT TIP 2026-09-06 (dev 87104c6281) on this item's own 9-repo cohort, full surveys, cold caches (jokij_dstref_09062026/measure.sh + readback.py; population = production taint._is_taint_call_edge, unresolved arm = is_resolved False or a dst whose node is an external boundary). RE-SCOPED, not closed: the number the filing said must be measured before choosing a fix -- the RECOVERABLE subset per analyzer, as opposed to the sentinel rate -- is now measured, and it says the sentinel is mostly the honest answer.\n\ndst_ref coverage on the unresolved arm, by language (08-04 in brackets):\n    language     unresolved   no dst_ref   coverage   (08-04)\n    python          56,259       27,687      50.8%    (50.7%)\n    javascript      24,555       23,326       5.0%    (57.7%)   <- denominator, not lost refs: since 08-04 the cohort's unresolved arm grew 62,861 -> 109,441, and bf8e138dac (\"every javascript instance-method call emits an edge\") is the commit that added the untyped-receiver method calls that were previously not emitted at all (js today: 22,527 sentinel METHOD edges); the 08-04 per-language absolute counts were not recorded, so this is consistent-with, not measured-against\n    go              23,272        4,572      80.4%    (72.6%)\n    typescript       2,948        2,091      29.1%    (96.9%)\n    java               824          428      48.1%    (23.9%)\n    bash               677            0     100.0%   (100.0%)\n    rust               438          319      27.2%    (34.1%)\n    swift              421          390       7.4%    (16.2%)   INV-kotob: the present-but-wrong 42% is gone (WI-gudak)\n    jsonnet             39            0     100.0%   (100.0%)\n    fish / powershell    8            8       0.0%     (0.0%)\n    TOTAL          109,441       58,821      46.3%    (60.4%)\n  Every dst_ref=None edge but two is the `external` sentinel in the path slot (58,819 of 58,821), i.e. _derive_dst_ref_from_id's WI-huzuv refusal, as filed.\n\nWHAT THE dst_ref=None EDGES ARE. METHOD calls, overwhelmingly: python 27,687 of 27,687, javascript 22,527 of 23,326, typescript 2,081 of 2,091, go 4,518 of 4,572, java 388 of 428, rust 261 of 319. The bare-FUNCTION residue is small and language-shaped: swift 333 (`Data`, `URL`, `Array` -- Foundation/stdlib constructors), javascript 799, rust 58 (`Ok`, `clap_complete::generate_to`), java 40, fish/powershell 8 (a bare command in a shell IS the sentinel's honest cell there, as bash's 100% shows from the other side). Samples: `x.toString()`, `resp.get()`, `w.WithLabelValues()`, `os.exit` via a Jest mock -- receivers whose type the analyzer does not know.\n\nTHE RECOVERABLE SUBSET, by the only evidence an analyzer could have put in the ref -- a receiver type hint or a module hint in meta: of 58,821 dst_ref=None edges, 1,595 carry a receiver type hint at all (python 363, javascript 1,027, java 146, typescript 40, swift 16; go carries `receiver` = a variable/field-chain name on 3,068, which is not a type). Split by whether the hint names a PROJECT symbol (a class in the map -- a symbol, not a module, so refusing a module_path is correct per INV-kotob/ADR-0051) or a type NOT in the map (external -- the only cohort where a module could have been named): python 363 project / 0 external; java 145 / 1; swift 16 / 0; typescript 3 / 37; javascript 92 / 935. So the recoverable subset is 973 edges, 1.7% of the None cohort, and 935 of them are javascript.\n\nREADING. An unresolved METHOD call on a receiver whose type the analyzer does not know (`x.toString()`, `resp.get()`, `w.WithLabelValues()`) has NO module recoverable from the call site at any cost short of type inference; ADR-0037's refusal to fabricate one is correct there, and INV-kotob's swift fix (WI-gudak, closed today) shows the cost of doing it right: swift's coverage FELL from 16.2% to 7.4% because the present-but-wrong 42% is now absent. So the 6x spread in the filing is not \"five analyzers forgot to name the module\"; it is the share of each language's unresolved calls that are untyped-receiver method calls (javascript 5931 of 5933, python all, typescript 2081 of 2091, go 4518 of 4572) versus bare function calls whose module an import can name (bash and jsonnet at 100% because a bare command IS its module). The emission gap this item can still own is the hinted cohort where the hint names an EXTERNAL type and the analyzer emitted the sentinel anyway -- 973 edges, 1.7% of the None cohort: javascript 935, typescript 37, java 1 -- and that is small enough to be per-analyzer follow-ups, not a family fix.\n\nWHAT CHANGES FOR THE THREE CONSUMERS THE FILING NAMED. WI-lonad's re-key, ADR-0037's string-parse retirement and io_boundary's module matching are bounded by the untyped-receiver share, which is a property of the CODE, not of the emission; the dst-string fallback therefore stays as a documented cell (the `external` sentinel = \"unidentified reference\", WI-huzuv), and this item's title should say so. The javascript `node:` import/call spelling split found today (WI-fiham) is the one fresh EMISSION defect in this family and is filed on its own.\n\nPROPOSED DISPOSITION for the owner: re-title to \"the `external` sentinel is the honest cell for untyped-receiver calls; per-analyzer emission gaps are the hinted-external residue (973 edges, 1.7% of the None cohort: javascript 935, typescript 37, java 1)\"; keep P2 only if the hinted residue is worth chasing; otherwise P3."  # 468b
